From 6af2066a92472be0a9aae8d23bdf0d071a6711e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:36:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] http/qt: optional custom SpotPass server

Adds a SpotPass group to Configure > General > Network (under Network /
Room): "Nintendo SpotPass" (default, unchanged behaviour) or "Custom
SpotPass server" with an address field.

With a custom server, http:C requests for Nintendo's SpotPass hosts
(npdl.cdn.nintendowifi.net content, nppl.c.app.nintendowifi.net policy
list, npul.c.app.nintendowifi.net uploads) are rewritten to the custom
address, keeping the original path and query. Without a scheme, https
is assumed. The original host is sent as X-Tangelo-Original-Host so one
server can serve all three. Each redirect is logged at Info level.

This works for both LLE and HLE BOSS, since both download through
http:C, which doesn't verify server certificates.

New settings: use_custom_spotpass_server, spotpass_server_url
([WebService] group; also read on Android).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
